sec.p:
The breathing segment extraction algorithm is shown in Algorithm 1. Remember that the trajectory distance of the Channel State Information ratio Qilij(fk,t) on the subcarrier fk moving on the complex plane from the moment t0 to the moment t0+Δt is ΔL=∫t=t0t=t0+ΔtddtQilij(fk,t)ds. We assume that the set of transition phase moments identified by the algorithm is T={t0+Δt1,t0+Δt2,…,t0+Δtm,…,t0+Δtn}, where Δtm is an integer multiple of Δt and is the minimum time interval considered by the algorithms in this section, and according to Algorithm 1 the signal Silij(fk,t)∈Rn characterizing respiration is obtained from the sequence Qilij(fk,t).
Algorithm 1 Breathing Segment Extraction Algorithm
Input: Q=Qi,li,jfk,t0,…,Qi,li,jfk,t0+Δt,…,Qi,li,jfk,t0+n×Δt Output: S=Si,li,jfk,t0+Δt,Si,li,jfk,t0+2×Δt,…,Si,li,jfk,t0+n×Δt 1:
Initialize an all-zero sequence S of length n with initialization flag=1. 2:
Step 1: Fit Q, using a spline curve to obtain a smoothed CSI ratio sequence Q^. 3:
Step 2: 4:
for i=2 to n do 5:
ΔQ^=Q^ilij(fk,t0+i×Δt)−Q^ilij(fk,t0+(i−1)×Δt) 6:
θ=arctan(Re(ΔQ)Im(ΔQ^)) 7:
if θ>23π then 8:
T=T∪{t0+i×Δt} 9:
end if 10:
end for 11:
Step 3: 12:
for i=2 to n do 13:
if (t0+i×Δt)∈T then 14:
flag=−flag 15:
end if 16:
Calculate the length of the smoothed CSI ratio moving trajectory on the complex plane from moment t0+(i−1)×Δt to moment t0+i×Δt: ΔL=∫t=t0+(i−1)×Δtt=t0+i×ΔtddtQ^ilijfk,tds 17:
Update S: S[i]=S[i−1]+flag×ΔL 18:
end for 19:
return S
